cases?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T13:44:08-08:00","id":1423816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1423749-aberrant-core-the-relation-between-quantum-flux-and-\u201ctalent-flux\u201d?p=1423812#post1423812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is even worse when we use Crossover, such as in an Aberrant party in which there are one or more Talent players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A Talent would never refers to Flux, even a in the general game you hardly talks about Talent Flux, Inspiration would be the term used both in game and in the rules usually, so It\u2019s not really a big deal.<br /> <br /> But I agree it\u2019s not a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T14:01:35-08:00","id":1423822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a perfect practical example of why using the same word makes everything very confusing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> This is even worse when we use Crossover, such as in an Aberrant party in which there are one or more Talent players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>I agree!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26537,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","user":"Jonnes.Derik","date":". 11-14-2020, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T14:32:55-08:00","id":1423831,"title":"","content":"What the core book calls flux actually refers to the difference between two parallel realities that a talent can tap into. I would be inclined to call <i>that</i> \u201cPotential\u201d \u2014 a term which has both a physics meaning (e.g., every location in a field has a Potential rating; and the difference in the Potentials of two points in the field is the amount of work you can accomplish by trying them together) and a narrative meaning (someone or something's potential is how much they're capable of; so Talent with access to a lot of Potential should be able to do far more than one who doesn't). <br /> <br /> Someone with a lot of Inspiration (the permanent rating) would have access to a lot of Potential (what's currently called Inspiration's associated pool of expendable points, e.g., \u201cspend Inspiration to\u2026\u201d would become \u201cspend Potential to\u2026\u201d). <br /> <br /> This leaves Flux as Quantum Flux.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T15:13:23-08:00","id":1423845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1423749-aberrant-core-the-relation-between-quantum-flux-and-\u201ctalent-flux\u201d?p=1423831#post1423831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the core book calls flux actually refers to the difference between two parallel realities that a talent can tap into. I would be inclined to call <i>that</i> \u201cPotential\u201d \u2014 a term which has both a physics meaning (e.g., every location in a field has a Potential rating; and the difference in the Potentials of two points in the field is the amount of work you can accomplish by trying them together) and a narrative meaning (someone or something's potential is how much they're capable of; so Talent with access to a lot of Potential should be able to do far more than one who doesn't).<br /> <br /> Someone with a lot of Inspiration (the permanent rating) would have access to a lot of Potential (what's currently called Inspiration's associated pool of expendable points, e.g., \u201cspend Inspiration to\u2026\u201d would become \u201cspend Potential to\u2026\u201d).<br /> <br /> This leaves Flux as Quantum Flux.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great idea!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T17:19:12-08:00","id":1423887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1423749-aberrant-core-the-relation-between-quantum-flux-and-\u201ctalent-flux\u201d?p=1423766#post1423766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct.<br /> <br /> &quot;Flux&quot; is the subtle energies of probability that ripple between parallel dimensions, subconsciously manipulated by Talents.<br /> <br /> &quot;Quantum Flux&quot; is the collective term for the energies of the four fundamental forces: the strong and weak nuclear forces, gravity, and electromagnetism. It's consciously manipulated by novas to dramatic effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>And my much earlier &quot;Hey, maybe we should call one of these things both called Flux something else&quot; gets a little love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-15T07:37:39-08:00","id":1424011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1423749-aberrant-core-the-relation-between-quantum-flux-and-\u201ctalent-flux\u201d?p=1423831#post1423831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the core book calls flux actually refers to the difference between two parallel realities that a talent can tap into. I would be inclined to call <i>that</i> \u201cPotential\u201d \u2014 a term which has both a physics meaning (e.g., every location in a field has a Potential rating; and the difference in the Potentials of two points in the field is the amount of work you can accomplish by trying them together) and a narrative meaning (someone or something's potential is how much they're capable of; so Talent with access to a lot of Potential should be able to do far more than one who doesn't).<br /> <br /> Someone with a lot of Inspiration (the permanent rating) would have access to a lot of Potential (what's currently called Inspiration's associated pool of expendable points, e.g., \u201cspend Inspiration to\u2026\u201d would become \u201cspend Potential to\u2026\u201d).<br /> <br /> This leaves Flux as Quantum Flux.</div> </div> </div> </div>I LOVED this idea!!! Kudos!!! <b>Potential </b>is a <b><i>perfect</i> </b>name.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}